# Line-ending policy — LF in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# Why: core.autocrlf is unset on this machine, so git could not tell that the
# working tree (CRLF) matched HEAD (LF). `git status` reported 20 phantom
# "modified" files while `git diff -w` and `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` were
# both empty — which made the "confirm git status clean" session-start rule
# untrustworthy. This file makes the comparison deterministic.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-side artifacts: never text, never normalized.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.node binary

# SQLite runtime state is binary and must never be line-ending converted.
*.db binary
*.db-shm binary
*.db-wal binary

# Lockfiles and generated artifacts: leave bytes exactly as written.
package-lock.json -text
*.tsbuildinfo -text